"""Real OpenBOR openborconstant() name -> value table.

Sourced 2026-08-23 from DCurrent/openbor (github.com/DCurrent/openbor,
the current actively-maintained OpenBOR engine repo -- this project has no
local copy of the exact ~2013-vintage source Double Dragon Moto (build 4432)
was built against, but openborscript's ANI_*/ATK_*/TYPE_* enum orderings and
bitflag values are a long-standing engine ABI mod authors depend on for
cross-version script compatibility -- they are not expected to have changed
across versions, unlike e.g. new natives being added at the end).

engine/openbor.h:
  - e_animations enum (ANI_NONE=0, sequential after) -- extracted
    programmatically from the real enum body, not hand-counted.
  - e_attack_types enum (ATK_NONE=MAX_INT is its own case, excluded;
    ATK_NORMAL=0, sequential after, MAX_ATKS/STA_ATKS are sentinels,
    excluded).
  - e_entity_type enum (bitflags, explicit shifts in source).
engine/source/globals.h: MIN_INT = (int)0x80000000.

**Scope boundary, load-bearing**: real openborconstant() also serves a
SECOND, incompatible use -- per-model DYNAMIC name lookups
(engine/source/openborscript/constants.c's ICMPSCONSTA/B/C macros),
e.g. `ANI_FOLLOW57` does NOT name a fixed enum member at all (only
ANI_FOLLOW1-4 are real enum entries) -- for n>4 the real engine indexes
into that SPECIFIC model's own `animfollows[]` array from its data file.
Same pattern for ATK_NORMAL11+ (STA_ATKS-relative), and per-model
DIE/PAIN/FALL/RISE/etc. suffix families beyond their own fixed slots.
This project's engine has no equivalent per-model animation-array
concept in its WRAM layout, so those names can NEVER be compile-time
constants here -- compile_call() must reject them with a clear error,
not silently return a wrong number. Only names that are REAL, FIXED enum
members (present in the tables below) are safe to fold at compile time.

**Also out of scope here**: PLAYER_MIN_Z/PLAYER_MAX_Z. These look like
constants but are real mutable globals in engine/openbor.c (default 160/
232, overridable per-level) -- not a fixed value openborconstant() could
safely fold at compile time even if this project tracked a Z axis at all
(it doesn't -- see the standing jump-Z-axis gap).
"""

OPENBOR_CONSTANTS = {}

